instrument wingie
; under the bridge: the Wingie's microphones listen to a place and the place becomes the sound.
; Mode 1 (a quick tap) captures the room: tap it, then clap, stamp or knock once, and for a
; quarter of a second the bridge is recorded; from then on everything the mics hear sounds
; inside it. fader1 (Mix) is how much of the bridge, fader3 (Volume) how loud.
; The left LED follows the mics, the right one what comes out. Best on headphones.

the bridge
----------
the arch is convolve 1
the drift is lfo
the walker is binaural
mic.both -> arch
mode1.tap -> arch.capture
fader1 -> arch.mix
arch -> walker
drift.saw -> walker.azimuth        ; the sound walks slowly round your head
fader2 -> drift.rate
walker.left -> left
walker.right -> right
mic.both -> lights.left
arch -> lights.right

the tonal skeleton
------------------
; only the strongest partials of the traffic, sung again as sines, then each one echoed at its
; own time. Hold Mode 2 to freeze the skeleton; the left keys transpose it.
the bones are resynth 2
the echoes are spectraldelay 1 curve=rising
the field is ambi
mic.both -> bones
keys1.pitch -> bones.pitch
mode2 -> bones.freeze
fader1 -> bones.partials
bones -> echoes
fader2 -> echoes.feedback
echoes ~> field
bones -> field
the slow is lfo
slow.sine -> field.azimuth
field.left -> left
field.right -> right
bones -> lights.left
echoes -> lights.right

the drier room
--------------
; the same place with its reverberation taken away (fader1 down: wetter, up: drier),
; and the hiss under it gated off: only the events stay
the dry is deverb
the clean is specgate
the ear is crossfeed
mic.both -> dry
fader1 -> dry.amount
dry -> clean
fader2 -> clean.threshold
clean -> ear.in1 ear.in2
ear.left -> left
ear.right -> right
dry -> lights.left
clean -> lights.right
